            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The multioutput-process "chlor-alkali electrolysis, mercury cell" delivers the co-products "chlorine, gaseous, mercury cell, at plant", "sodium hydroxide, 50% in water, mercury cell, at plant" and "hydrogen, liquid, mercury cell, at plant". The allocation is done according to the masses of the different products - i.e. 46.4% chlorine - 52.3% sodium hydroxide and 1.3% hydrogen.;
